{"key": "bb04e8f3ea1b6777", "role": "operator", "t": 1790990079.781, "seconds": 5.583, "output": "```python\ndef check_similarity(PURPOSE, Date):\n    # Assuming the condition is that both PURPOSE and Date are not empty and have some similarity\n    if PURPOSE and Date:\n        # For simplicity, let's assume similarity means they have at least one common word\n        purpose_words = set(PURPOSE.split())\n        date_words = set(Date.split())\n        if purpose_words.intersection(date_words):\n            return 1\n    return 0\n\n# Test the function\nPURPOSE = \"Meeting Report\"\nDate = \"Meeting Schedule\"\nprint(check_similarity(PURPOSE, Date))\n```"}
